Timing templates:

-T0 (paranoid): Extremely slow and stealthy. Minimal packets, long delays (up to 5 minutes between probes). For IDS evasion on highly sensitive networks.

-T1 (sneaky): Still slow and stealthy, but slightly faster than T0. Good for avoiding detection.

-T2 (polite): Slower, reduces load on the target. Less aggressive than default, still cautious.

-T3 (normal): Default setting. Balanced speed and reliability, suitable for most scans.

-T4 (aggressive): Faster, assumes a good network. Common for pentesting when time matters.

-T5 (insane): Very fast, sacrifices accuracy for speed. Best for large networks or when you’re in a hurry.